      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "From a sociological perspective, gentle parenting fosters a fragile dependency, failing to equip children with the resilience needed for the harsh realities of an unforgiving society. The constant removal of natural consequences creates a sheltered environment where children never learn the critical skill of self-regulation under pressure. This coddling, in effect, cultivates a generation ill-prepared for the competitive, high-stakes environment of modern life. Ultimately, it substitutes genuine character development with performative emotional appeasement.",
      "source": "target",
