      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Authoritative parenting, which demands respect and sets clear, non-negotiable limits, is fundamentally about teaching competence and self-control. Conversely, the gentle approach prioritizes immediate emotional comfort over long-term behavioral mastery. The traditional model instills the necessary internal locus of control, teaching children that actions have predictable, meaningful outcomes. Therefore, the authoritative framework objectively builds capable, disciplined individuals ready to navigate the world, whereas gentle parenting cultivates emotional fragility.",
      "source": "target",
